  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "In an electronics store, the ratio of the number of cell phones to the total number of gadgets sold (cell phones and computers) is $\\frac{8}{11}.$ If $16$ cell phones were sold in a week, how many computers were sold?",
  "worked_solution": "We are given that the ratio of the number of cell phones sold to the number of gadgets (cell phones and computers) sold is $\\frac{8}{11}.$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of cell phones sold and the denominator represents the number of cell phones and computers sold.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $16$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{8\\times 2}{11\\times 2}=\\frac{16}{22}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the number of cell phones and computers sold that week was $22.$ Of this amount, the number of computers sold was\n\n$$\n22-16=6.\n$$",
